From: OpenIRD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mips: mm: do not build with -Werror

arch/mips/mm is built with -Werror.  The code was warning-free for the
compilers of its day, but the pinned gcc 4.9.4 has warnings that did not
exist then, and here they stop the build:

  include/asm/elf.h:235:7: error: "__MIPSEL__" is not defined [-Werror=undef]
  arch/mips/mm/c-r4k.c: error: variable 'tmp' set but not used
                               [-Werror=unused-but-set-variable]
  arch/mips/mm/init.c:  error: variable 'lastpfn' set but not used

None of them is a defect in what the code does (the first is a big-endian
build evaluating "#elif __MIPSEL__", the others are leftovers), so let them
be warnings like everywhere else in the tree instead of touching each site.

Origin: gpl-derived
---
--- a/arch/mips/mm/Makefile
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/Makefile
@@ -31,5 +31,3 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_R5000_CPU_SCACHE)  += sc-r5k.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_RM7000_CPU_SCACHE)	+= sc-rm7k.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_MIPS_CPU_SCACHE)	+= sc-mips.o
-
-EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Werror
